    "q-184234": {
      "dom_id": "step-q184234",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Prove that $3n+4$ is even provided that $n$ is even.\n\nIf $n$ is even, then $n=\\,${{field-1}} for {{field-2}}.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+4 & ={{field-3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-4}}. Since $a$ is {{field-5}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-6}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+4 & ={{field-7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $3n+4$ is {{field-8}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall the following:\n\n- If an integer $n$ is even, then there exists an integer $p$ such that $n=2p.$\n\n- If an integer $n$ is odd, then there exists an integer $q$ such that $n=2q+1.$\n\nIn this case, we need to prove the following:\n\n$$\nn\\text{ is even}\\,⇒\\,3n+4\\text{ is even}\n$$\n\nWe start by using the fact that $n$ is even.\n\nIf $n$ is even, then $n=2a$ for some integer $a.$\n\nThe idea is to substitute $n=2a$ into the expression $3n+4$ and show it is even by writing it as a multiple of $2.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+4 & =3(2a)+4 \\\\  & =6a+4 \\\\  & =2{{(3a+2)}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we define another integer $b=3a+2$ (highlighted above), we have that $3n+4=2b,$ which shows that $3n+4$ is indeed a multiple of $2.$\n\nLet $b=3a+2.$ Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+4 & =2{{(3a+2)}_{⏟}}_{b} \\\\  & =2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$\n\nFinally, we write our conclusion.\n\nTherefore, $3n+4$ is even.\n\nPROOF\n\nIf $n$ is even, then $n=\\,$$2a$ for some integer $a$.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+4 & =2(3a+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ $3a+2$. Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+4 & =2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $3n+4$ is even.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
